      "title": "Clippers docked five first-round draft picks and fined $30m over Kawhi Leonard scandal",
      "link": "https://www.theguardian.com/sport/2026/sep/02/la-clippers-kawhi-leonard-fine-salary-cap-nba",
      "description": "<ul><li><p>Team circumvented salary cap rules to sign star</p></li><li><p>Owner Steve Ballmer lands one-year ban</p></li></ul><p>The NBA has handed down one of the biggest punishments in the history of the league to the Los Angeles Clippers after finding that the franchise <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/sport/2025/sep/03/clippers-deny-claims-star-forward-kawhi-leonard-was-paid-28m-for-job-that-didnt-exist\">circumvented salary cap rules</a> when it courted Kawhi Leonard as a free agent.</p><p>The league has stripped the team of five first-round draft picks, giving the team no natural pick in the draft from 2029 through 2033.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/sport/2026/sep/02/la-clippers-kawhi-leonard-fine-salary-cap-nba\">Continue reading...</a>",
      "source_name": "The Guardian World",
      "published": "2026-09-02T20:52:28"
    },
    {
      "title": "Steve Ballmer banned by NBA over improper payment to basketball star",
      "link": "https://www.ft.com/content/6b74303c-0190-4e86-8a7b-feaf3dd29658?syn-25a6b1a6=1",
